From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fulton Engineering Services <noreply@fultonengineeringservices.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ucp_device: allow host memory in local mem list params check

GB10 (Grace+Blackwell) has no GPUDirect RDMA — the NIC can only DMA
from host memory, not GPU VRAM.  NIXL EP works around this by
allocating the RDMA buffer with cudaMallocHost (page-locked host
memory) and registering it as DRAM_SEG.

The UCX GPU device API (ucp_device_local_mem_list_create) rejects
host memory because ucp_device_local_mem_list_params_check requires
memh->sys_dev to match the GPU's local_sys_dev.  Host memory has
sys_dev = UCS_SYS_DEVICE_ID_UNKNOWN, which never matches.

Relax the check to also accept UCS_MEMORY_TYPE_HOST.  The IB
transport can still register host memory via ibv_reg_mr (that is
standard host RDMA), and the GPU can access it over NVLink, so the
transfer itself is correct — only the sys_dev guard was too strict.

---
 src/ucp/core/ucp_device.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ucp/core/ucp_device.c b/src/ucp/core/ucp_device.c
--- a/src/ucp/core/ucp_device.c
+++ b/src/ucp/core/ucp_device.c
@@ -398,7 +398,8 @@
         }
 
-        if (memh->sys_dev != local_sys_dev) {
+        if ((memh->sys_dev != local_sys_dev) &&
+            (memh->mem_type != UCS_MEMORY_TYPE_HOST)) {
             ucs_error("mismatched local sys_dev for element=%zu", i);
             return UCS_ERR_UNSUPPORTED;
         }
-- 
